<title>AUSTRIA: Libya says return of Iraq oil will not hit price.</title>
<headline>Libya says return of Iraq oil will not hit price.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Libyan oil minister Abdullah Salem al-Badri said on Monday that the possible return of Iraqi oil to the market should not depress the oil price.</p>
<p>&quot;I think nothing would happen (to the price) because the Iraqi quantity is not that much,&quot; Badri said. &quot;We think the market can absorb the additional quantity.&quot;</p>
<p>On the issue of quota busting he said there was a &quot;moral obligation&quot; on all OPEC members to abide by their quotas.</p>
<p>When asked when Iraq should be allowed to export oil he said &quot;tommorrow.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Vienna Newsroom +431 713 2034</p>
